title: Grilled Portobello
method: grill
source: https://www.americastestkitchen.com/recipes/662-gas-grilled-marinated-portobello-mushrooms
protein: none
ingredient_count: 4
---

Combine @olive oil{1/2%cup}, @lemon juice{3%tbsp}(from 1 lemon), @garlic{6%medium cloves}(minced fine, about 2 tablespoons), and @table salt{1/4%tsp} in large #zipper-lock plastic bag{}.

Add @portobello mushrooms{4}(each 5 to 6 inches or about 6 ounces each, stems removed and discarded, caps wiped clean); seal bag and gently shake to coat mushrooms with marinade.

Let stand at room temperature until seasoned, ~{1%hour}.

Meanwhile, cut four 12-inch-square pieces of @foil{}; when mushrooms are almost done marinating, turn all burners on #gas grill{} to high, close lid, and heat grill until hot, ~{10-15%minutes}.

Remove mushrooms from marinade.

Place a foil square on work surface and set mushroom on top, gill-side up; fold foil edges over to enclose mushroom and seal edges.

Scrub rack with #wire grill brush{}.

Grill mushrooms, with sealed side of foil packet facing up, until juicy and tender, ~{7-9%minutes}.

Using #tongs{}, unwrap mushrooms and discard foil; set unwrapped mushrooms on rack gill-side up and cook until grill-marked, ~{30-60%seconds}.

Remove from grill and use in one of following recipes.